{"step_index":63,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T13:53:44Z","content":"I have thoroughly inspected and assimilated the architecture, conventions, and operational rules of **`infra-management-system`**.\n\nHere is the comprehensive diagnostic and repository status report:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Repository Overview & Mission\n* **Role**: Ansible Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) repository governing the **OMT / SFR Caraïbe** infrastructure (Nginx frontends, PHP-FPM pools, MariaDB clusters, ProxySQL topologies, DotNet / CGR Core apps, NFS HA / DRBD storage, Docker, and TLS lifecycle management).\n* **Upstream GitLab**: `gitsi.intranet.local/omt/infra/management/infra-management-system` (Project **#144**).\n* **Deployment Engine**: **Semaphore** (`semaphore.corp.intranet.local`, Project *Infra Management* ID **1**). Deployments track the `main` branch. Direct ad-hoc `ansible-playbook` runs on production targets are strictly prohibited.\n\n---\n\n### 2. The Non-Negotiable Production Rules (Règles Dures)\nI have locked the critical safety invariants into memory:\n1. **Zero Downtime**: Additive changes only (new vhosts, new pools, new users). Never alter running shared configurations (e.g., shared ProxySQL instances).\n2. **Reload, Never Restart**: Always enforce `state: reloaded` for Nginx and PHP-FPM. Never inject `state: restarted`.\n3. **No File Deletion**: Read and append only on repository and target hosts (scratch permitted strictly under `/tmp`).\n4. **Loïc's Explicit Authorization**: Every Semaphore task (`run_task`) and any command touching production (`trp-*p-*`) requires coup-par-coup human sign-off.\n5. **Never Trust Semaphore `--check` / `dry_run`**: Verified on 2026-07-24 (`trp-efaliap-cmp1`) that `--check` failed to simulate and applied modifications live. Any production change **must** be preceded by an explicit read-only reconnaissance playbook (`recon-*.yml` with `changed_when: false`).\n6. **Corporate SSL Push**: Always bypass schannel issues with `git -c http.sslBackend=openssl push`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Semaphore Runner Topology\n\n| Runner Tag *(Case-Sensitive)* | Runner Host | Target Environment |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `dev` | `th2-ansid-run1` | Development |\n| `val` | `th2-ansiv-run1` | Validation |\n| `CORP` | `th2-ansic-runner1` (`th2-awxc-ap1`) | Corporate network |\n| `PROD` | `th2-ansip-run1` (`172.30.199.225`) | Production |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Git & Working Tree Status\n\nWhen inspecting the terminal output:\n\n```text\nOn branch main\nYour branch is up to date with 'origin/main'.\n\nUntracked files:\n  (use \"git add <file>...\" to include in what will be committed)\n\t.claude/agents/\n\tAGENTS.md\n\nnothing added to commit but untracked files present\n```\n\n* **Branch Status**: <span style=\"color:green\">**Active / Clean**</span> (Green) on `main`, synchronised with `origin/main` at commit `838bad7` (*Merge branch 'le-cert/postfix.outremer-telecom.fr-20260817124644'*).\n* **Untracked Elements**: <span style=\"color:#d4a017\">**Untracked / Pending**</span> (Yellow):\n  * [`.claude/agents/koby-kamek-infra.md`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/.claude/agents/koby-kamek-infra.md) (the dedicated Claude agent definition for this repo).\n  * [`AGENTS.md`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/AGENTS.md) (guidelines file for OpenCode/Antigravity agents).\n* **Stashes**: None active.\n\n---\n\n### Ready for Next Action\nWhether you need a read-only reconnaissance playbook (`recon-*.yml`), a syntax validation check, or an investigation into a specific inventory or role (`roles/`, `inventories/`), what is our target today?","thinking":"**Defining Infrastructure's Purpose**\n\nThe `infra-management-system` repository's core is Ansible-based Infrastructure-as-Code. This IaC manages diverse environments: production, validation, corporate, and development. The infrastructure includes Nginx, PHP-FPM, MariaDB, ProxySQL, .Net applications, NFS HA clusters, Docker, and TLS certificate management.\n\n\n"}
