{"step_index":91,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T13:56:06Z","content":"**Yes, absolutely.** \n\nI have full programmatic access to the Semaphore instance at `https://semaphore.corp.intranet.local` (Project **Infra Management**, ID `1`). \n\nI verified the connection and authentication against the Semaphore API:\n* **API Status**: <span style=\"color:green\">**200 OK**</span> (Authenticated via token with internal corporate CA bundle).\n* **MCP Integration**: Configured in [`~/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json`](file:///home/koby/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json) utilizing the local binary `/home/koby/.local/bin/semaphore-mcp`.\n\n---\n\n### How I Can Interact with Semaphore\n\n1. **Inspect Templates & Inventories**:\n   - List and search templates, associated playbooks (`playbooks/*.yml`), runner tags, and required survey variables.\n   - Inspect previous task runs, outputs, and commit hashes.\n2. **Trigger Tasks**:\n   - Launch a task on a specific template (with custom commit hash, message, or survey variables).\n3. **Monitor Execution & Logs**:\n   - Track live task progression and report final status (<span style=\"color:green\">**success**</span>, <span style=\"color:#d4a017\">**running**</span>, or <span style=\"color:red\">**failed**</span>) with complete Ansible log outputs.\n\n---\n\n### Critical Guardrails (Repo & Production Rules)\n\nBefore triggering any task, remember our rules of engagement:\n* **Non-Prod (`dev`, `val`, `CORP`)**: I will specify the exact template ID, target environment, and arguments before triggering.\n* **Production (`PROD` / `trp-*p-*`)**:\n  * **Strictly gated**: No task targeting production will be executed without **Loïc's explicit confirmation**.\n  * **Recon first**: If the task modifies production, a read-only reconnaissance playbook (`recon-*.yml` with `changed_when: false`) must be reviewed first, because Semaphore's `--check`/`dry_run` cannot be trusted as a safeguard.\n\n---\n\nWhich template would you like to inspect or trigger? You can give me the template name or ID, or describe the playbook you want to run!","thinking":"**Verifying Execution Prerequisites**\n\nThe rules mandate zero downtime, no file deletion, and a distrust of dry runs. Crucially, any production execution requires explicit approval. A clear plan description and confirmation from the user are also necessary before any modifying action.\n\n\n"}
